codex
The final literature check disqualifies the family despite the harness verdict. Our “balanced” construction gives every vertex exactly three neighbours in each other planted class, so the two class-indicator directions are exact adjacency eigenvectors with eigenvalue \(-3\). Linear algebra recovers the colour partition in polynomial time whenever that eigenspace is isolated; more broadly, published work gives polynomial recovery for expanding graphs with pseudorandom balanced colourings. This violates H. I will not ship an empirically hardened but theoretically easy generator; I’m replacing the deliverable with an explicit rejection report.
