+
+</details>
+
+`verify(inst, inst["answer"])` returns `(True, "ok")`. Dropping its last jump returns `(False, "wrong jump count: expected 37, got 36")`.
+
+## Gate results
+
+| gate | result |
+|---|---|
+| G1 planted verifies | 12/12 preset/seed checks |
+| G2 corruption | 5/5 rejected with 5 distinct reasons |
+| G3 round trip | fenced, prose-surrounded response parsed and verified |
+| G4 structured guessing | 0/200,000 hits; sampled uniformly from proper-phase sequences |
+| G5 exact sparsity | 6 proper colourings; `6/3^12 = 1.1290e-5` structural fraction |
+| G6 adversaries | degree outlier 0/8, greedy 0/8, 32-restart DSATUR 0/8; degree spread 0 |
+| G7 scaling | doubled `n=360`, 1,802 vertices and 721 jumps, planted answer verified |
+| G8 canonical key | 120/120 invariance and carried-witness checks; 20/20 unrelated keys distinct; exact canonical branch 20/20 |
+
+The machine-readable measurements are in `selftest_report.json`.
+
+## Oracle hardening loop
+
+The official harness verdict is `hardened`, shipping `medium` after one escalation. Timeout rows are retained but were not scored.
+
+| preset | model | seed | solved? | reason |
+|---|---|---:|---|---|
+| easy | GPT-5.6 Terra | 468847831 | yes | parsed witness verified `ok` |
+| easy | Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview | 1808783731 | yes | parsed witness verified `ok` |
+| easy | Claude Sonnet 5 | 267595525 | yes | parsed witness verified `ok` |
+| medium | Claude Sonnet 5 | 1424129599 | no | used 32,000 completion tokens and emitted no content (`length`) |
+| medium | Grok 4.6 | 1611063746 | error | 900 s deadline; redrawn, not scored |
+| medium | Grok 4.6 | 1878378065 | error | 900 s deadline; redrawn, not scored |
+| medium | GPT-5.6 Terra | 751596886 | no | explicitly returned no answer |
+| medium | Gemini 3.1 Pro Preview | 806835976 | no | parsed sequence violated independence at jump 20 |
+
+Full replies and timings are in `llm_loop_transcript.jsonl`; the pool, master seed, and verdict are in `.meta.json`.
+
+## Use
+
+From this directory:
+
+```python
+import gen_2408_04743 as gen
+
+params = gen.DIFFICULTY[gen.SHIPPING_DIFFICULTY]
+inst = gen.make_instance(seed=123, **params)
+question = gen.render(inst)
+candidate = gen.parse_answer(model_output)
+ok, reason = gen.verify(inst, candidate)
+```
+
+Run the gates with `python3 gen_2408_04743.py`. From the repository root, emit 20 fresh shipping instances with:
+
+```bash
+bash scripts/emit.sh 2408.04743 20 medium
+```
+
+## Caveats
+
+- NP-hardness is for the containing worst-case relation; there is no formal average-case hardness proof for these random degree-six, equitably 3-colourable graphs. A specialised recovery algorithm could invalidate the family.
+- G4's 0/200,000 estimate uses the strongest obvious prior: correct shortest-path phases, one choice per auxiliary vertex, and uniformly random colours. It is not a statistical proof that the true probability is below `1e-6`, nor a claim about heuristic or learned priors. The raw jump-pair space is much larger and is not used to claim resistance.
+- The panel did not try full exponential DSATUR/backtracking, SAT/ILP solvers, spectral partition recovery, or modern long-run local search. It tested only degree/label outliers, deterministic greedy colouring, and 32 randomized DSATUR restarts.
+- Density is delicate: degree four was easy for local search, while denser planting can reveal or rigidly force the hidden partition. Only six-regular auxiliary graphs ship.
+- One of the three decisive oracle failures is completion-budget exhaustion rather than a wrong witness; Terra declined to answer, while Gemini supplied the directly checkable invalid witness. The harness nevertheless counts all three according to its fixed rules.
+- `canonical_key` is exact when invariant refinement individualises all vertices, as it did in 20/20 tests. If refinement leaves ties, the documented fallback is isomorphism-invariant but incomplete and can collide on non-isomorphic graphs.
